<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Publishing Readiness Audit, Phase 7 — replaces the previous blanket
  android:usesCleartextTraffic="true" (flagged as VULN-DATA-02, Critical, in
  doc/Audit/01_Security_Data_Protection_Audit.md).

  Default posture: cleartext (unencrypted HTTP) traffic is now DENIED for every
  domain. All of this app's real traffic already uses HTTPS (YouTube Data API,
  YouTube embeds, OpenStreetMap tile server), so this should require zero
  further changes for normal operation.

  Note on the RTMP "Local OBS" testing feature (rtmp_ip_dialog.dart): RTMP is not
  HTTP, and Android's Network Security Config governs HTTP(S)/socket traffic made
  through Android's own network stack (HttpURLConnection, OkHttp, WebView) — it
  does not apply to flutter_vlc_player's own RTMP networking. If a real device
  test shows local RTMP preview breaking after this change, that's independent
  of this file and would need investigating in the VLC player adapter instead —
  don't loosen this config to "fix" an RTMP issue without confirming that first.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
